      "schema:text": {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "in paragraph (a), by inserting after the words \"section 77(1)\" the words \"or 77(1A)\". Amendment of section 103"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/1999/31/eng@/~part_II__cl_8",
      "@type": "akn:clause",
      "eli:number": "8",
      "hasPart": [
        "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/1999/31/eng@/~part_II__cl_8__para_b",
        "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/1999/31/eng@/~part_II__cl_8__para_c"
      ],
      "isPartOf": "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/1999/31/eng@/~part_II",
      "schema:name": {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Section 103 of the principal Act is amended -"
      },
      "schema:text": {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "the words \", other than a company to which section 103A applies,\";"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/1999/31/eng@/~part_II__cl_8__para_b",
      "@type": "akn:paragraph",
      "eli:number": "b",
      "isPartOf": "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/1999/31/eng@/~part_II__cl_8",
      "schema:text": {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "in subsection (2), by inserting after the word \"assessed\" the words \", other than a company to which section 103A applies,\"; and"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/1999/31/eng@/~part_II__cl_8__para_c",
      "@type": "akn:paragraph",
      "eli:number": "c",
      "isPartOf": "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/1999/31/eng@/~part_II__cl_8",
      "schema:text": {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "by deleting subsection (7). New section 103A"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/1999/31/eng@/~part_II__cl_9",
      "@type": "akn:clause",
      "eli:number": "9",
      "isPartOf": "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/1999/31/eng@/~part_II",
      "schema:text": {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "The principal Act is amended by inserting after section 103 the following section: \"payment 103A. (1) This section shall apply only to companies. (2) Except as provided in subsection (3), tax payable under an assessment for a year of assessment shall be due and payable on the due date whether or not that company appeals against the assessment. (3) Where an assessment is made under section 91, 92 or 96A, or where an assessment is increased under section 101(2), the tax payable under the assessment or increased assessment shall be due and payable on the service of the notice of assessment or composite assessment or increased assessment, as the case may be, on the company assessed whether or not that company appeals against the assessment or increased assessment. (4) Where any tax due and payable under subsection (2) has not been paid by the due date, so much of the tax as is unpaid upon the expiration of that date shall without any further notice being served be increased by a sum equal to ten per cent of the tax so unpaid, and that sum shall be reccverable as if it were tax due and payable under this Act. (5) Where the tax due and payable has been increased under subsection (4), any balance remaining unpaid upon the expiration of sixty days from the due date shall without any further notice being served be further increased by a sum equal to five per cent of the balance unpaid, and that sum shall be recoverable as if it were tax due and payable under this Act. (6) Subject to subsection (8), where any tax due and payable under subsection (3) has not been paid within thirty days after the service of the notice, so much of the tax as is unpaid upon the expiration of that period shall without any further notice being served be increased by a sum equal to ten per cent of the tax so unpaid, and that sum shall be recoverable as if it were tax due and payable under this Act. (7) Where the tax due and payable has been increased under subsection (6), any balance remaining unpaid upon the expiration of sixty days from the date of such increase shall without any further notice being served be further increased by a sum equal to five per cent of the balance unpaid, and that sum shall be recoverable as if it were tax due and payable under this Act. (8) Where any tax is payable in accordance with subsection (3), the Director General may allow the tax to be paid by instalments in such amounts and on such dates as he may determine and in the event of default in payment of any one instalment on the date specified for payment the balance of the tax then outstanding shall be due and payable on that date and shall without any further notice being served be increased by a sum equal to ten per cent of that balance, and that sum shall be recoverable as if it were tax due and payable under this Act. (9) Where the tax due and payable has been increased under subsection (8), any balance remaining unpaid upon the expiration of sixty days from the date of such increase shall without any further notice being served be further increased by a sum equal to five per cent of the balance unpaid, and that sum shall be recoverable as if it were tax due and payable under this Act. (10) Subsections (6) and (7) shall apply (with any necessary modification) in relation to a debt due and payable under section 108(5) or 108(7) as it applies in relation to tax due and payable on the service of the notice in accordance with subsection (3). (11) Notwithstanding the foregoing subsections, where tax due and payable is increased by a sum under subsection (4), (5), (6), (7), (8) or (9), the Director General may in his discretion for any good cause shown remit the whole or any part of that sum and, where the amount remitted has been paid, the Director General shall repay the same. (12) For the purposes of this section, \"due date\" means the last day of the sixth month from the date following the close of the accounting period.\". Amendment of section 106"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/1999/31/eng@/~part_I__cl_1",
      "@type": "akn:clause",
      "eli:number": "1",
      "hasPart": [
        "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/1999/31/eng@/~part_I__cl_1__subsec_1",
        "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/1999/31/eng@/~part_I__cl_1__subsec_2",
        "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/1999/31/eng@/~part_I__cl_1__subsec_3",
        "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/1999/31/eng@/~part_I__cl_1__subsec_4",
        "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/1999/31/eng@/~part_I__cl_1__subsec_5"
      ],
      "isPartOf": "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/1999/31/eng@/~part_I"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/1999/31/eng@/~part_I__cl_1__subsec_1",
      "@type": "akn:subsection",
      "eli:number": "1",
      "isPartOf": "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/1999/31/eng@/~part_I__cl_1",
      "schema:text": {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "This Act may be cited as the Income Tax (Amendment) (No. 2) Act 1999."
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/1999/31/eng@/~part_I__cl_1__subsec_2",
      "@type": "akn:subsection",
      "eli:number": "2",
      "isPartOf": "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/1999/31/eng@/~part_I__cl_1",
      "schema:text": {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "This Act comes into operation on 1 January 2000 and, except as proyided in subsections (3), (4) and (5), shall have effect for the year of assessment 2001 and subsequent years of assessment."
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/1999/31/eng@/~part_I__cl_1__subsec_3",
      "@type": "akn:subsection",
      "eli:number": "3",
      "isPartOf": "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/1999/31/eng@/~part_I__cl_1",
      "schema:text": {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Subsection 107c(3) which is introduced by section 12 of this Act shall have effect for the year of assessment 2002 and subsequent years of assessment."
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/1999/31/eng@/~part_I__cl_1__subsec_4",
      "@type": "akn:subsection",
      "eli:number": "4",
      "isPartOf": "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/1999/31/eng@/~part_I__cl_1",
      "schema:text": {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Sections 13,14,15 and 16 shall have effect upon the coming into operation of this Act."
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/1999/31/eng@/~part_I__cl_1__subsec_5",
      "@type": "akn:subsection",
      "eli:number": "5",
      "isPartOf": "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/1999/31/eng@/~part_I__cl_1",
      "schema:text": {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Section 17 shall have effect only for the year of assessment 2001."
      }
    }
  ]
}
